WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.790
- So the Trump indictments are here,

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:04.730
but they're not the ones
that most people expected.

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.460
On July 1st, Donald Trump's
chief financial officer,

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:08.293
Allen Weisselberg,

00:00:08.293 --> 00:00:10.210
surrendered after Manhattan
District Attorney,

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.970
Cy Vance, charged Weisselberg
and the Trump organization

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:16.690
with 15 criminal offenses
including conspiracy,

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.910
grand larceny, criminal tax
fraud, and falsifying records.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.407
The indictment alleges a, quote,

00:00:21.407 --> 00:00:23.330
"sweeping and audacious payment scheme,"

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.670
that allowed Weisselberg and others

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.320
be paid more compensation

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:29.630
than the company taxpayers
reported to tax authorities.

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:32.630
The charges center on unpaid
taxes on employee benefits

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.730
that Weisselberg and his
family allegedly received.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.870
The benefits include things
like free apartments,

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:41.530
cash bonuses, comped Mercedes cars,

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:43.700
and private school tuition for his kids.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.870
And after the announcement,
many of Trump's critics rejoiced

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.890
with many reminiscing about
the time that Al Capone went

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:50.920
to prison for tax evasion
rather than for murder,

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.670
and the #LockHimUp trended
on Twitter all morning.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:55.990
So is this really it?

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:58.640
Is the hammer really truly
about to fall on Donald Trump,

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.340
his company, his
associates, and his family?

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:02.924
Well, it depends.

00:01:02.924 --> 00:01:06.650
(triumphant instrumental music)

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:07.483
Hey, Legal Eagles.

00:01:07.483 --> 00:01:08.316
It's time to think

00:01:08.316 --> 00:01:09.980
like a white collar
criminal defense attorney

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:13.320
because former president Trump
waged a year's long battle

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.760
with Cy Vance over subpoenas
into his tax records.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:18.480
When the Supreme Court
ruled that Trump had

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.530
to turn over his tax information to Vance,

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:23.700
he and New York Attorney
General Letitia James announced

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:26.560
that they were collaborating
on several investigations.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.560
But the Vance indictments
don't have anything

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.470
to do with Trump's personal taxes

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:33.450
or at least the way that
he values his properties.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:34.440
So the question is,

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.360
is the Weisselberg
indictment the opening salvo

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:39.480
in a bigger war over Donald
Trump's tax avoidance strategies

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.470
and are the feds coming next?

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:45.020
And also, can Weisselberg
himself beat this rap?

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:46.900
Well, today, I'm going to
shed light on what we know

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.820
about the Trump organization case.

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:50.120
Of course, keep in mind as always,

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:52.700
this is just an indictment,
and nothing has been proven

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.080
against either Weisselberg
or the Trump organization.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.750
Both he and the company
have pleaded not guilty

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.270
to these criminal charges.

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:01.580
So to get into this, let's
establish some basic things

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:03.180
about the area of tax law.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.150
Employees and corporations pay taxes

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:07.130
on an employee's compensation.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:09.360
In addition to salary,
compensation includes things

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.030
like tuition, housing, and cars

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.950
if the employer provides
them, and under the tax code,

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:16.020
these are classified as fringe benefits.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:17.260
According to the IRS,

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:20.590
any fringe benefit that
you receive as an employee

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:23.380
is taxable and must be
included in the recipient's pay

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:25.700
unless the law specifically excludes it.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.970
Employers can deduct employee compensation

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:29.340
from the taxes that they owe,

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:30.870
but they still have to pay Medicare

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.590
and social security
taxes to the government.

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:34.330
These are payroll taxes.

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:36.780
Generally, the employer pays
half of the payroll taxes,

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:38.580
and the employee pays the rest.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.830
Now, if a corporation can
find a way to classify some

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:43.750
of the employee compensation
as a deductible expense,

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:46.850
it avoids the payroll taxes
saving approximately 14%

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:48.330
that would've gone to the government.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.100
This also pays off for the employees

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:53.090
since disguising compensation
as a routine business expense

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:56.300
avoids not only the payroll
taxes but also the income taxes

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.520
that would be owed by the employee.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:00.860
Now here, prosecutors allege
the Trump organization

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:03.270
has been engaged to defraud federal state

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:06.430
and local tax authorities
starting as far back as 2005.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:07.840
The scheme was two pronged.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:09.700
First, it involved allowing employees

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.940
to dramatically understate
their compensation

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.680
so they could pay less tax.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.050
This also allowed the
company to obtain tax refunds

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:19.350
on taxes already deducted
and paid to tax authorities.

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:21.800
Second, the company has failed
to withhold income taxes

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.350
on wages, salaries, bonuses,

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:25.020
and other forms of compensation,

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:27.310
allowing allegedly the Trump organization

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.250
to evade the payment of payroll taxes

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.360
that the organization was required to pay

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.680
in connection with employee compensation.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.280
As the indictment explains,
no one benefited more

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:39.220
from this alleged tax evasion
scheme than Allen Weisselberg,

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:41.780
who was in charge of
the company's finances.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.470
Weisselberg is firmly enmeshed

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:45.230
in the Trump organization's business.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:47.230
Former Trump fixer Michael
Cohen told Congress

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:48.650
that Weisselberg helped him pay

00:03:48.650 --> 00:03:51.200
off adult film star Stormy
Daniels and other women

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.930
who had affairs with Trump.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.790
Cohen also testified
that he and Weisselberg,

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.560
quote, "concocted phony valuations,

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:57.890
the company's real estate holdings

00:03:57.890 --> 00:04:00.880
that suit Mr. Trump's
needs at any given moment."

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:03.420
Weisselberg was also a key
person in the investigation

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.140
over the misuse of the charitable funds

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.940
by the Donald J. Trump Foundation,

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:09.140
which resulted in Trump himself admitting

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.870
that he used charity funds to buy things

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:13.760
for his golf clubs and
presidential campaigns.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.610
And the Trumps paid $2 million

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.560
to settle the case and are now barred

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.430
from chartering another
nonprofit in New York.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:22.500
Many expected Trump to pardon Weisselberg,

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.280
but he did not do so.

00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:26.830
Now the Manhattan DA alleges
that Weisselberg was able

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:28.863
to, quote, "receive indirect
employee compensation

00:04:28.863 --> 00:04:31.580
from the Trump organization
in the approximate amount

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:34.580
of $1.76 million."

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.250
The indictment alleges
that the Trump companies

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:38.210
helped Weisselberg get paid in ways

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.130
that helped the companies
avoid reporting it

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:41.370
to tax authorities.

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:42.640
So let's talk about the first count

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:44.280
against Weisselberg and
the corporate defendants,

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.670
which was a scheme to defraud in violation

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:49.700
of New York penal code section 190.65.

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:51.480
A person is guilty of a scheme to defraud

00:04:51.480 --> 00:04:53.087
in the first degree, if he or she, quote,

00:04:53.087 --> 00:04:56.530
"engages in a scheme constituting
a systemic ongoing course

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:58.760
of conduct with intent to defraud more

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:01.210
than one person or
obtain property for more

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:03.770
than one person by false
or fraudulent pretenses,

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.770
representations, or promises,
and so obtains property

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:09.360
with a value in excess of $1,000

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:11.110
from one or more such persons."

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.680
Now this isn't usually an offense

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:14.310
that's charged as a single count.

00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:15.660
It's usually charged in connection

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.560
with other offenses, as it is here.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:19.600
And in essence, a felony scheme to defraud

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:21.110
is basically an accusation that someone

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:24.130
was running some kind of scam
with the intent to steal.

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.080
And when Weisselberg and his wife moved

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:29.200
into a Trump building on
Riverside Boulevard in 2005,

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:31.120
the Trump organization paid their rent,

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.440
the garage, and four utilities.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:34.510
According to the DA,

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:36.670
the expenses constituted
employee compensation

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:38.300
and taxable income to Weisselberg.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:41.310
And in an almost cartoonish
example of tax evasion,

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:44.240
these payments involved some
extremely tricky bookkeeping.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.730
The DA claims that "these
payments were not booked

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:48.400
to the Trump organization's general ledger

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:50.990
as employee compensation
but were instead labeled

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:51.937
and deducted as," quote,

00:05:51.937 --> 00:05:54.200
"'rent expense' in the general ledger.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.170
However, for certain years,
the Trump organization

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:59.510
maintained internal that
tracked the amounts it paid

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:02.330
for Weisselberg's rent,
utility, and garage expenses."

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:03.460
So did you catch that?

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:06.310
The Trump organization allegedly
kept two sets of books,

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:07.960
one with the fake numbers and one

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:10.280
with the real figures paid to Weisselberg.

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:12.380
The indictment says that
when the Trump corporation

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:13.740
paid Weisselberg's rent,

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:15.270
someone from the Trump organization

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:18.330
reduced Weisselberg's salary
by a corresponding amount.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:20.800
If this is true, this is
extremely strong evidence

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:22.627
of intent that makes it
much harder for Weisselberg

00:06:22.627 --> 00:06:24.420
and the corporation to argue that it

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:26.470
was all an accident or misunderstanding.

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:27.750
- We know what we're gonna do?

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:29.330
- Till the gunman indicts, anyway.

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.270
- Now people who are
skeptical about the charges

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:32.690
have suggested the tax authorities

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:35.410
are attacking the Trump
organization for political reasons,

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:37.690
and one way to prove that
would be to show that people

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:40.330
are rarely prosecuted for
this kind of tax fraud.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:43.090
However, people do go to
jail for the same conduct

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:44.540
that Weisselberg is accused of.

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:48.090
In fact, one of Trump's
old pals, Leona Helmsley,

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:50.170
was sentenced to four years in prison

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:52.020
for having her real estate company pay

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.700
to renovate her Greenwich
mansion and then failing

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:56.950
to report those payments as income.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:58.700
The man who prosecuted Helmsley was,

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:01.660
and I'm not kidding you,
Rudy Giuliani. (laughs)

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:03.330
By the time that Helmsley was charged,

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:04.780
she and Trump had a falling out,

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:06.080
and Trump celebrated the charges

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:07.287
with a letter calling her, quote,

00:07:07.287 --> 00:07:09.030
"a disgrace to the industry

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.650
and a disgrace to humanity in general."

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:13.270
And there's more.

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:16.300
The DA said that from 2005 to 2013,

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:18.810
Weisselberg pretended not to
be a resident of New York City

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:21.040
in order to avoid paying city taxes.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.100
Weisselberg listed his
home in upstate New York

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:25.320
as his permanent residence
all while spending most

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:27.280
of his time living and working in the city

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:29.460
that the Trump organization
allegedly paid for.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:32.530
And this is a common scheme
to evade paying local taxes,

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:36.310
and, in fact, in another
similar situation,

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:39.040
Derek Chauvin, yes, the former
Minneapolis police officer

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:40.780
convicted of murdering George Floyd,

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:42.770
was actually charged with
aiding and abetting tax fraud

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:44.520
in Washington County, Minnesota.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.490
Chauvin and his wife claimed
to be legal residents

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:48.400
of Florida while Chauvin worked full-time

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.260
as an officer in Minnesota.

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:52.300
The couple then filed tax returns claiming

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:53.770
to be Florida residents.

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:56.430
Now the district attorney also
claims that Trump employees,

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:58.870
including Weisselberg,
arranged for tuition expenses

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:00.590
for Weisselberg's family members.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:03.350
This money was allegedly
paid by personal checks drawn

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:06.520
on the account of and
signed by Donald J. Trump.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:08.087
The DA says that these payments, quote,

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:09.650
"constituted employee compensation

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:11.357
and taxable income to Allen Weisselberg

00:08:11.357 --> 00:08:13.970
and was treated as part of
Weisselberg annual compensation

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:16.530
and internal records maintained
by the Trump corporation."

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:19.010
So once again, the real
compensation was included

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:20.980
in a secret ledger of
payments to Weisselberg

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:23.320
but not included on Weisselberg's W2 forms

00:08:23.320 --> 00:08:25.200
or reported to tax authorities.

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:27.090
And the companies did
withhold income taxes

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:29.580
on the tuition payments, and
Weisselberg allegedly failed

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:32.940
to report about $359,000
in tuition expenses

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:34.400
for family members.

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:36.830
And Donald, Jr. has seemingly
admitted that his father

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.640
was aware of in part of this arrangement.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:41.060
- It's not 1.7 million. That's income.

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:46.060
The taxable portion of that
to New York state is 8%.

00:08:46.083 --> 00:08:50.203
That's $136,000 over 16 years.

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:52.770
That's 10 grand a year.

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:54.840
Half of that, because
my father's a good guy,

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:58.430
he paid for this guy's
grandchildren's education.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:02.090
Our tax experts say
that's not even taxable.

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:03.940
- All right, so a couple
of things stand out here.

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.660
It seems the legal strategy
of the Trump family

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:07.800
is to say that whatever
Weisselberg was doing,

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:09.750
Trump was not aware of it,
but he may have been aware

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:11.510
of it because he's such a nice guy,

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:14.640
but also this is all
Weisselberg's responsibility

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:16.210
because he's the CFO.

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:18.900
So we can listen to former
president Trump in his own words.

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:23.163
- Or education for your
grandchildren. I don't even know.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:26.490
Does anybody know the
answer to that stuff?

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:28.890
- And so far, others have
reported and Don, Jr.

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:31.310
has confirmed that these
checks were written

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:34.540
by Donald Trump, Sr. personally

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.370
for Weisselberg's compensation.

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:38.570
And even if Trump was
personally signing the checks,

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:40.920
which reports indicate
that he was doing even

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:45.920
as late as 2017, he'll
claim that he signs hundreds

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:48.700
if not thousands of checks a month,

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:50.410
and that's just part of doing business.

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:53.990
So he, again, would be relying on his CFO,

00:09:53.990 --> 00:09:56.980
Allen Weisselberg, who
obviously was the bad actor

00:09:56.980 --> 00:09:58.960
in this particular case.

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:00.270
Whether a jury would believe that

00:10:00.270 --> 00:10:01.940
or not is an open question.

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:03.010
These things are hard.

00:10:03.010 --> 00:10:06.060
It's hard to prove these tax prosecutions.

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:08.450
And the statements from Don,
Jr. seem to be a preview

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:09.650
of a defense that we're going to see

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:11.340
down the line because any amount

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:14.540
of tuition reimbursement
that exceeds $5,250

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:16.690
is considered a fringe benefit of the job.

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:18.680
So it seems like he's arguing
that although the tuition

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.700
is around $10,000 a year,
Trump, Sr. only paid

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:23.950
for half of that, making it non-taxable.

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:26.350
And of course, one can pay for tuition.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:28.510
That's fine, but the
tuition can't be claimed

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:31.020
as a deductible business
expense if it's not.

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:32.490
Additionally, the indictment alleges

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:34.730
that the Trump companies
paid annual lease expenses

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:37.630
on two Mercedes-Benzes
that were the personal cars

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:39.250
of Weisselberg and his wife.

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:41.150
The end result was that
neither the corporation

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:43.920
or Weisselberg paid taxes on $196,000

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:45.560
in compensation for the cars.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:47.870
The Trump organization
also gave Weisselberg

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:51.910
over $29,000 in cash to
distribute as holiday bonuses.

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:54.120
The company allegedly
wrote checks to an employee

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:56.730
and had that employee give
the cash to Weisselberg.

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:58.600
The Trump corporation
allegedly booked this cash

00:10:58.600 --> 00:10:59.890
as holiday entertainment

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:02.280
but maintained internal
spreadsheets showing the cash

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:05.140
to be part of Weisselberg's
employee compensation.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:08.350
Of course, no taxes were reported or paid.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:10.040
So according to this, the Trump executives

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:11.690
weren't even hiding what they were doing.

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:13.610
They kept track of it all on a spreadsheet

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:15.920
in complete confidence so
the IRS would never know.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:19.170
It was allegedly right
there in black and white.

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:20.890
And then there's a whole
slew of allegations

00:11:20.890 --> 00:11:22.730
regarding ad hoc personal expenses.

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:24.930
Weisselberg's compensation
allegedly included payment

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:27.700
of expenses on homes and apartments used

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.200
by Weisselberg's family.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:30.990
This was for things like carpet,

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:33.340
new beds, giant TVs, and furniture.

00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:34.697
The Trump companies meticulously, quote,

00:11:34.697 --> 00:11:36.910
"tracked the payment of
the expenses internally

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:38.870
as part of Weisselberg's
annual compensation."

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:41.450
And the same set up was
used to pay the expenses

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:42.660
and rent of other employees,

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:44.730
including two of
Weisselberg's family members.

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:46.010
Although these people aren't named,

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:47.940
the "New York Times" reported
that Weisselberg's children

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:50.450
also benefited from the
association with Trump.

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:52.220
Weisselberg's son Barry got a job

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:54.470
with the Trump organization
managing the Wollman Rink

00:11:54.470 --> 00:11:56.670
in Central Park and played DJ

00:11:56.670 --> 00:11:58.350
for the Trump Christmas parties.

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:02.137
Yes, real shades of
"Succession's" cousin Greg.

00:12:02.137 --> 00:12:04.000
Egg, Greg. I don't know.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.520
And then we have bonuses,

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:07.820
and speaking of the Wollman skating rink,

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:09.780
the indictment alleges
that the Trump companies

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:12.170
used subsidiaries to
pay some executives end

00:12:12.170 --> 00:12:14.410
of the year bonuses that
were then misreported

00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:17.200
as non-employee compensation,
violation of federal law.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:19.360
The companies playing along with a scheme

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:21.820
included the Wollman Rink,
Trump International Golf Club,

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:24.940
Mar-a-Lago Trump Las
Vegas Development, LLC,

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:25.773
and other entities.

00:12:25.773 --> 00:12:28.110
This corporate sleight of hand
allegedly allowed Weisselberg

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:30.540
and others to receive
non-employee compensation

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:32.110
that allowed them to participate

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:34.620
in a tax-deferred pension
plan that otherwise

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:35.700
wouldn't have been available

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:37.050
as an employee of the Trump organization.

00:12:37.050 --> 00:12:38.800
And the district attorney says

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.800
that Weisselberg knowingly
falsified records

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:41.930
in furtherance of the scheme.

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:43.930
He repeatedly reported
that his compensation

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:48.290
was fixed at 940,000, quote,
"comprised of $540,000

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:51.680
in base salary and 400,000
in end of the year bonuses."

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:53.910
But Vance says that the Trump corporation

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:55.980
at Weisselberg's direction "excluded

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:57.700
from his reported gross income the amounts

00:12:57.700 --> 00:12:59.260
that were paid to him indirectly."

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:01.230
So the rent, cars, cash, furniture,

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:04.190
and tuition were purposefully
hidden from tax authorities.

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:05.400
And then there are a whole raft

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:07.250
of other interesting related charges.

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:09.170
Weisselberg was charged with conspiracy

00:13:09.170 --> 00:13:10.890
to commit second-degree larceny.

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:11.990
Generally, for this kind of claim,

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:13.610
a prosecutor has to show three things

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:14.590
to prove this conspiracy,

00:13:14.590 --> 00:13:17.570
which in and of itself
is not a separate charge.

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:19.320
First, you have to show
that the involvement

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:21.410
of two or more people;
second, the criminal intent,

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:22.890
which means people must know that they

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:25.250
are doing something illegal; and third,

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:27.150
at least one of the conspirators has

00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:29.430
to take overt action in
furtherance of the conspiracy.

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:31.170
And one of the interesting
things about this charge

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:32.880
is that it brings us back to the return

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:35.540
of unindicted co-conspirator number one.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:36.720
It's been a while since we've heard

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:38.020
about this particular character.

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:40.750
And in earlier seasons of
"As the Trump World Turns,"

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:42.800
Robert Mueller presented a long report

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.510
describing potentially
criminal acts committed

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:46.210
by individual number one,

00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:48.590
and Michael Cohen went
to jail for conspiracy

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:51.400
with unindicted co-conspirator number one.

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:55.250
Both of these people are
presumed pretty obviously

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:57.650
to be Donald Trump, but
in this particular case,

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:00.730
individual one may not
actually be Donald Trump.

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:03.070
In fact, many have reported
that the most likely candidate

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:05.640
for this particular unindicted
co-conspirator number one

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:08.820
is Trump organization
comptroller Jeff McConney.

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.420
But what was this conspiracy about?

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:13.307
Well, the district attorney
says that from, quote,

00:14:13.307 --> 00:14:15.760
"at least 2005 through the
date of this indictment,

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:17.030
the named defendants and others,

00:14:17.030 --> 00:14:19.120
including unindicted
co-conspirator number one,

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:21.640
agreed to an implemented
the compensation scheme

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:23.290
with the object of enabling Weisselberg

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:25.520
to underreport his income
to federal authorities

00:14:25.520 --> 00:14:26.840
and thereby evade taxes

00:14:26.840 --> 00:14:29.070
and falsely claim federal tax refund,

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:30.430
to which he was not entitled.

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:32.380
As a result of the conspirators' actions,

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:33.640
during the period of the conspiracy,

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:36.707
Weisselberg took approximately $94,900."

00:14:36.707 --> 00:14:39.020
And to satisfy the requirements
of the conspiracy law,

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.530
the indictment lays forth the
overt acts that Weisselberg

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:44.610
and others allegedly took in
furtherance of this conspiracy.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.500
I'm not gonna read them
to you, but you can see

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:48.730
that the acts include
underreporting income,

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:51.850
and, effectively, many people
were involved in scheme.

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:54.320
Then there are claims of grand larceny.

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:57.290
Prosecutors have a lot of
options in these kinds of cases

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:59.070
for charging people with the theft

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:01.090
of state money that
should have been taxed,

00:15:01.090 --> 00:15:03.270
including the charge of grand larceny.

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:05.250
So count three involves
the predicate offense

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:06.547
for the conspiracy grand larceny,

00:15:06.547 --> 00:15:09.240
and Weisselberg is charged
with second-degree larceny

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:12.620
in violation of penal code section 155.40.

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:15.060
A person is guilty of grand
larceny in the second degree

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:18.110
when he steals property
valued at more than $50,000.

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:20.310
And then there are the
criminal tax fraud claims.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:21.590
Counts four, five, six,

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:24.420
and seven charged the Trump
corporations and Weisselberg

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:26.640
with third and fourth
degree criminal tax fraud.

00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:28.900
A person commits criminal
tax fraud in the third degree

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:31.770
if they performed a,
quote, "tax fraud act."

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:33.970
The tax code of New
York defines a tax fraud

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:36.410
as "intentionally providing
materially false information

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.960
on a tax return or during a tax audit

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:41.310
or failing to intentionally pay taxes owed

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:42.810
to the state of New York.

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:44.640
The defendant's actions
must be intentional

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:45.900
with the intent to defraud,

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:48.110
and the defendant must
have defrauded the state

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:50.400
for at least a one-year
period in the amount greater

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:53.293
than $10,000 but not more than $50,000."

00:15:53.293 --> 00:15:55.680
And then there are the counts
related to falsifying records.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:58.100
Counts eight through
15 are for various acts

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.840
of falsifying business records.

00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:01.660
Weisselberg is charged with four counts

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:03.580
of offering a false instrument for filing,

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:07.600
a violation of New York penal code 175.35.

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:10.270
He's specifically charged
with a first-degree felony.

00:16:10.270 --> 00:16:12.500
The prosecution here has to prove first

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:14.320
that he knowingly offered
a written document

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:17.670
or instrument that contains
a false statement on its face

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:20.480
and presented it, quote,
"to a public authority,

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:22.390
public servant, or public office."

00:16:22.390 --> 00:16:24.780
Second, the prosecution has to
show the document was filed,

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:26.810
registered, or became a party

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:29.240
of that particular office's records,

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:31.240
and third, this is a felony crime

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:33.500
if the person acts with
the intent to defraud.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:36.180
And while the intent to defraud
is a complicated concept,

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:38.150
in New York, it's been
interpreted as an act

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:40.470
or behavior where the
goal is to lead another

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.680
into error or disadvantage.

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:44.670
This doesn't necessarily
mean that the person needed

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:45.860
to present a false document

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:47.410
for the purpose of stealing money.

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:49.380
It's enough to show that the
defendant wanted to interfere

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:51.600
with the government's ability
to administer the law.

00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:54.080
And the Trump corporations
and Weisselberg are charged

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:56.180
with falsifying business
records in the first degree

00:16:56.180 --> 00:16:59.690
in violation of penal code section 175.10,

00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:01.460
which states, quote, "A person is guilty

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:03.640
of falsifying business
records in the first degree

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:06.060
when he commits the crime of
falsifying business records

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:08.150
in the secondary end when his intent

00:17:08.150 --> 00:17:10.920
to defraud includes his
intent to commit another crime

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:13.720
or to aid or conceal in
the commission thereof."

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.790
The defendants were accused
of fraud in connection

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:18.480
with three years of
filing Weisselberg's W2's,

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:20.550
and the 15th count is
particularly interesting

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:22.670
because it alleges that
the Trump organization

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:26.330
and Weisselberg acted to
basically cover up their tracks.

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:29.210
Manhattan district attorney
general counsel Carey Dunne

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:31.210
provided additional information
during the arraignment.

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:34.020
Quote, "The CFO himself
directed the company records

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:36.940
be deleted to conceal his
participation in the scheme.

00:17:36.940 --> 00:17:39.320
Even now, there's been no
attempt to impose discipline

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:41.630
on the people involved,
to report the crimes,

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:44.410
to repay the proceeds,
or even to amend any

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:45.650
of the false tax returns.

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:48.070
Instead, when confronted
by our investigation,

00:17:48.070 --> 00:17:50.230
the company at its
highest levels decided not

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:52.300
to accept responsibility and to cooperate,

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.000
which is what companies do if they want

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:55.920
to be viewed as a good corporate citizen.

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:58.480
Instead, it forced us into
litigation for a year and a half,

00:17:58.480 --> 00:18:00.790
including two trips to the Supreme Court."

00:18:00.790 --> 00:18:03.100
Falsifying business
records in the first degree

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:05.270
is a class E felony, which
can result in prison time

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:08.430
but often results in just
probation, fines, and the like.

00:18:08.430 --> 00:18:10.610
On the other hand, maybe everyone
at the Trump organization

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.980
is just really bad at
taxes and accounting.

